INT. NIGHT-SHIFT CLEANING CLOSET - COUNTY BANK - NIGHT

Mop buckets. Bleach. A fluorescent tube ticking.

A WOMAN (50s, grey smock, hair in a net) hangs her coat on a hook. Steady hands. She hums.

She opens a locker. Name tape inside the door: "D. VASQUEZ-MOORE."

She lifts the false bottom. A drill. A thermal lance. Gloves.

Calm. Too calm.

She checks her watch. Presses play on a cheap recorder.

DOLORES (V.O.)
(recorded, her own voice)
If you're hearing this, the cameras loop at two. Do not rush. Mop first.

DOLORES nods along. Hums again.

She lifts the bucket. Wheels it out.

Hallway. Vault door at the end, gleaming.

She stops. Sets the mop against the wall.

DOLORES (CONT'D)
(to the door, softly)
Evening, old friend.

She pulls the lance from under the smock. Snaps the valve.

A hiss. A blue flame.

DOLORES (CONT'D)
Thirty years I've cleaned around you.

She starts to cut.
